body:
Trying to understand what's the status of this PR, as it looks abandoned (?).
It seems the PR as it is would return a dictionary like:

```
{
	"name": "Node",
	"brief_description": "Base class for all scene objects.",
	"description": "Nodes are Godot's building blocks...",
	"inherits": "Object",
	"methods": [
		{
			"name": "add_to_group",
			"description": "Adds the node to the [param group]...",
			"return_type": "void",
			"arguments": [
				{
					"name": "group",
					"type": "StringName"
				},
				{
					"name": "persistent",
					"type": "bool",
					"default_value": "false",
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
```

The problem is, if the dictionary changes structure in the future, then anyone depending on it breaks.
So it would preferred to have individual methods similar to what https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12531 proposes.

What would be the right place to continue discussing the potential implementation of this? here? https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12531?
